	(text "DESIGN NOTES (summary; full analysis in docs/stage2/sheet4-design-notes.md)\n1. Every X4 signal passes an SN74AVC4T774 (A = carrier +3V3). VCC isolation + Ioff: no back-feed when a side is off (C-29).\n   U401/U403/U404 carry RP2040 -> carrier inputs only; B = X4_3V3_REF (header 3.3 V, reference only: uA; ER-3).\n2. U402 carries EVERY carrier -> RP2040 output (IRQ_N, ATTN, MISO, TDO). Its /OE (RP_EN_N, from buffer U406) is low only\n   while Q401 (U405: GP24 > 0.940 x X4_3V3_REF) and Q402 (GP24 driven) both conduct. Model-derived disable latency <= 190 ns.\n   The X4's K4 key can cut IOVDD while the header 3.3 V stays up (Q32, [V S1 sh.21]) (S4-6 rev A3).\n3. U401 SPI (mode 0, GPIO chip select); U403 JTAG option (D-12: OE from a DIP switch, default isolated, so J201\n   on sheet 2 has priority); U404 four RP2040 LEDs (C-26). B-side 100k pull-downs on every RP2040 -> carrier input.\n4. Default resistors (R-51): CS_N high, SCK/MOSI low, MISO/ATTN low (not ready), IRQ_N 2.2k pull-up, strong\n   enough against the blank FPGA's weak pull-down (305 uA max: 2.6 V). Host-link pins use PULLMODE=NONE in the LPF.\n5. R411-R414 33R source terminations on the ribbon drivers (values TBV at layout). With U402 isolated and the RP2040\n   running, IRQ_N reads high through the RP2040's own GP22 pull-up (firmware FW-6) and ATTN low through R425.\n   Nothing on the carrier sources current into GP24 (R424 removed). Analysis: sheet4-s46-isolation.md.\n6. Not yet validated: an ERC-clean result does not imply electrical or timing correctness."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 300 0)
